WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.099
Grammar
Logic Series.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:03.312
Error one.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.603
Look at this
sentence:

00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:07.546
‘The furniture
are expensive.’

00:00:07.586 --> 00:00:09.836
It sounds fine,
but it’s wrong.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.243
Let’s find
out why,

00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:13.467
with logic,
not memorising.

00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:16.052
Here is the idea.

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:17.610
Some nouns
don’t name one

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.866
single thing.

00:00:18.906 --> 00:00:20.113
They name
a whole group

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.657
of things,
and the group acts

00:00:21.697 --> 00:00:23.009
as one unit.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:24.803
Let’s see it.

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:25.843
Here is a chair.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.886
Here is a table.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.919
A sofa. And a bed.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.193
Four different
things.

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:32.847
But English
doesn’t use four

00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:33.951
names here.

00:00:33.991 --> 00:00:35.755
It draws a circle
around them,

00:00:35.795 --> 00:00:37.309
and gives
the whole group one

00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:39.068
name: furniture.

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:42.386
So furniture
is not one object.

00:00:42.426 --> 00:00:43.803
It is one unit.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.529
And a unit
means one.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.881
One is always
singular.

00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:49.658
We can’t add
s to one.

00:00:49.698 --> 00:00:51.459
So there is no
‘furnitures’,

00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:53.916
and the verb must
be singular too.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.596
So the correct
sentence is:

00:00:56.636 --> 00:00:58.803
‘The furniture
is expensive.’

00:00:59.937 --> 00:01:01.270
Let’s prove
it again.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.742
A plate. A bowl.

00:01:02.782 --> 00:01:04.155
A mug.
Circle them,

00:01:04.195 --> 00:01:05.259
and name
the group:

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:07.495
crockery.
One unit, so:

00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:08.575
‘The crockery
is clean.’

00:01:08.615 --> 00:01:09.911
Never
‘crockeries’.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.244
One more. A fork.

00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:14.784
A knife. A spoon.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:15.563
Circle them:

00:01:15.603 --> 00:01:16.950
cutlery.
One unit, so:

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.587
‘The cutlery
is in the drawer.’

00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:21.199
And if you
need a number?

00:01:21.239 --> 00:01:22.389
Count the pieces,

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:23.474
not the unit:

00:01:23.514 --> 00:01:24.997
two pieces
of furniture,

00:01:25.037 --> 00:01:26.567
a piece
of cutlery.

00:01:27.503 --> 00:01:29.188
So remember
the logic:

00:01:29.228 --> 00:01:30.998
many things,
one circle,

00:01:31.038 --> 00:01:32.536
one unit,
one name,

00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:34.100
one singular verb.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.413
That’s error one.

